    "genre": "Environmental Economics",
    "difficulty": "IPMAT Advanced / CAT Standard",
    "passage": "In 1968, Garrett Hardin posed a thought experiment involving a pasture open to all local herdsmen. Each herdsman receives 100% of the financial gain from adding an extra animal, while the degradation of overgrazing is shared equally. However, Elinor Ostrom's research dismantled Hardin's tragic inevitability by proving that local communities can design self-organized polycentric governance without top-down state coercion or private enclosure.",
